<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Merovingian dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Merovingian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Merovingian dynasty was the first royal house of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>, ruling from the fifth century until 751. Its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis I</a> united much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. In its later period real power passed to the mayors of the palace, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a> deposed the last Merovingian king, founding the Carolingian dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/merovingian-dynasty.jpg" alt="Merovingian dynasty" width="320" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rudric · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Merovingian_dynasty-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
